 \n`SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` and restoring it afterwards. `writes a health record without the debug variable and keeps the skill label out` persists one record built \nwith `skillLabel: 'sk-doc'`, `errorDetails: 'probe detail'` and `degraded: true`, reads the one line at `advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(root)` and expects no \n`skillLabel`, no `errorDetails`, `degraded` true and `readAdvisorStatus({ workspaceRoot: root }).hookHealth?.invocations` 1. `trims the default health log to \n200 records` persists 301 records and expects 200 lines in that file. Verify: `V tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts \ntests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts tests/legacy/advisor-privacy.vitest.ts tests/metrics-file-permissions.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"- [ ] T012 [P] Write a health record by default and report its degraded share and age (`MET`, `STT`). In `AdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord`, add `readonly \ndegraded?: boolean`. In `createAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord`, add `readonly degraded?: boolean` to the input and spread `degraded: true` into the result only \nwhen `input.degraded === true`. In `validateAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord`, also require `record.degraded` to be `undefined` or a boolean. In \n`persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord`, serialize the record as it is when `process.env.SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` is set and otherwise a copy without `skillLabel` and \n`errorDetails`, and pass `{ requireDebug: false }` to `writeBoundedJsonl` in both cases. Add a comment saying a health record answers how the hook runs, which \nneeds no prompt, skill or error text, so it is written on every prompt, and the debug variable adds the two fields that say what the prompt was about. In \n`AdvisorHookHealthSection`, add `readonly rollingDegradedRate: number` and `readonly lastRecordAt: string | null`. In `buildAdvisorHookHealthSection`, set \n`rollingDegradedRate` to the share of `lastInvocations` whose `degraded` is true (0 when there are none) and `lastRecordAt` to the `timestamp` of the last \nelement of `lastInvocations`, or `null` when it is empty. In `STT`, add two cases after `reports hook health from durable diagnostic records`, each deleting \n`SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` and restoring it afterwards. `writes a health record without the debug variable and keeps the skill label out` persists one record built \nwith `skillLabel: 'sk-doc'`, `errorDetails: 'probe detail'` and `degraded: true`, reads the one line at `advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(root)` and expects no \n`skillLabel`, no `errorDetails`, `degraded` true and `readAdvisorStatus({ workspaceRoot: root }).hookHealth?.invocations` 1. `trims the default health log to \n200 records` persists 301 records and expects 200 lines in that file. Verify: `V tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts \ntests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts tests/legacy/advisor-privacy.vitest.ts tests/metrics-file-permissions.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '93p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/015-health-default-and-brief-refinements/tasks.md | fold -s -w 160\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794564760786,"end":1794564761752}}}}
